    "problem_statement": "Protocol switching with 101 Informational Response doesn't work\n\nDescription\n\nWhen attempting to upgrade a connection using the HTTP protocol switching mechanism with a 101 status code, the connection doesn't properly switch protocols.\n\nFor example, when a client sends a request with an Upgrade header:\n\n```\nGET / HTTP/1.1\nHost: example.com\nUpgrade: websocket\nConnection: Upgrade\n```\n\nAnd the server responds with a 101 status code:\n\n```\nHTTP/1.1 101 Switching Protocols\nUpgrade: websocket\nConnection: Upgrade\n```\n\nThe connection should switch to the new protocol, but it doesn't. The server continues to interpret subsequent data as HTTP instead of passing it through as raw data for the new protocol.\n\nThis affects WebSocket connections and other protocol upgrade scenarios where a 101 response is used to indicate the protocol switch."
